analysis:
### Vulnerability Analysis
In `Dapper.Rainbow`'s SQL Compact edition implementation (`Dapper.Rainbow/SqlCompactDatabase.cs`), the overridden `Insert(dynamic data)` method also constructs the SQL insert statement by joining dynamic, unsanitized property names/keys directly into the command string:
```csharp
var sql = "insert " + TableName + " (" + cols + ") values (" + colsParams + ")";
```
If an application uses SQL Compact Database provider with `DynamicParameters` or dictionaries built from untrusted inputs, an attacker can manipulate the property/parameter names to execute arbitrary SQL commands.

### Conceptual Exploit Payload
A dictionary with a malicious key can be supplied:
```csharp
var payload = new Dictionary<string, object>
{
    { "col) VALUES ('val'); DROP TABLE Users; --", "dummy" }
};
```
When processed, the resulting query structure results in raw SQL Injection.

